<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54229" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατᾰκονά</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακαίνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>destruction</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακονὰ ἀβίοτος βίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					821
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).--The v.l., supported by Sch. (cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				50.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				381.22
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακονᾷ . . βίος</span>,
			implies a Verb <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ-ᾰκονάω</span></b> ,
				<i>wear away</i>, as is done in whetting steel.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
